document.write('<STYLE type=text/css>div#rsstojs A:link {COLOR: ;font-family:arial; font-size:12;}div#rsstojs A:visited {COLOR: ;font-family:arial; font-size:12;}div#rsstojs A:hover {COLOR: ;font-family:arial; font-size:12;}div#rsstojs { COLOR:  ;font-family:arial; font-size:12; } p#rsslink { COLOR:  ;font-family:Arial; font-size:11; }</STYLE><div id=rsstojs style=background-color:;width:px; height:44px; align=><p class=channel ><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/3032113/ target=blank >NBCSports.com: Sports</a><br></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41522431/ns/sports-nba/ target=blank >Lakers spoil Allen&#39;s record night in Boston</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41522431/ns/sports-nba/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/g-spt-110210-kobe-ray-allen-810p.thumb.jpg alt=Lakers guard Kobe Bryant drives to the basket against Celtics guard Ray Allen during the second half Thursday night. Bryant scored 20 of his 23 points in the second half. style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Kobe Bryant scored 20 of his 23 points in the second half, and the Los Angeles Lakers spoiled Ray Allen&#39;s record-setting night by beating the Boston Celtics 92-86 in an NBA finals rematch on Thursday night.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41523037/ns/sports-nba/ target=blank >Celtics&#39; Allen sets all-time 3-point record</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41523037/ns/sports-nba/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/g-spt-110210-ray-allen-611p.thumb.jpg alt=Boston&#39;s Ray Allen celebrates after making a 3-pointer against the Lakers to set the NBA record for 3-point baskets during the first quarter Thursday night. style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Ray Allen broke the NBA record for 3-pointers on Thursday night, sinking two in the first quarter against the Los Angeles Lakers as the man he passed, Reggie Miller, sat courtside working the TV broadcast.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41522456/ns/sports-nba/ target=blank >Afflalo&#39;s shot snaps Mavs&#39; 10-game win streak</a><br/>Arron Afflalo hit a 19-footer at the buzzer and the Denver Nuggets beat the Dallas Mavericks 121-120 on Thursday, ending the Mavericks&#39; 10-game win streak.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41516697/ns/sports-nba/ target=blank >Sloan steps down as Jazz coach</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41516697/ns/sports-nba/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/jazz sloan resignation basketball--1162267823_v2.thumb.jpg alt=FILE - This Dec. 3, 2010, file photo shows Utah Jazz coach Jerry Sloan during the first half of an NBA basketball game against the Dallas Mavericks,  in Salt Lake City. A person with knowledge of the situation says Sloan is stepping down as head coach of the Jazz. The person also told The Associated Press on Thursday, Feb. 10, 2011,  that longtime assistant Phil Johnson also will resign.  (AP Photo/Colin E Braley, File) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Like the impressive mountains that dominate Salt Lake City&#39;s skyline, Jerry Sloan was a fixture in the Utah landscape.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41523389/ns/sports-college_basketball/ target=blank >St. John&#39;s rips No. 10 Connecticut</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41523389/ns/sports-college_basketball/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/spt-110210-uconnstjohns.thumb.jpg alt=St. John&#39;s Paris Horne and D.J. Kennedy block a shot by Connecticut&#39;s Kemba Walker. The Red Storm won Thursday&#39;s game, 89-72. style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Dwight Hardy scored a career-high 33 points and St. John&#39;s took command in the second half in an 89-72 victory over No. 10 Connecticut on Thursday night, the Red Storm&#39;s fourth win over a top-13 team this season at Madison Square Garden.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41523722/ns/sports-nhl/ target=blank >Staal sinks Kings with last-second OT goal</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41523722/ns/sports-nhl/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/spt-110210-penguins-kings.thumb.jpg alt=Pittsburgh&#39;s Brett Sterling celebrates his goal with teammate Dustin Jeffrey. Sterling helped the Penguins to a 2-1 win vs. the Kings on Thursday. style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Jordan Staal scored the winning goal with 18.4 seconds left in overtime to lift the Pittsburgh Penguins to a 2-1 win over the Los Angles Kings on Thursday night.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41494845/ns/sports-nhl/ target=blank >Duff: Unlikely Sid the Kid will ever be the same</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41494845/ns/sports-nhl/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/110106_sidney_crosby.thumb.jpg alt=The Penguins&#39; Sidney Crosby hasn&#39;t played since Jan. 5 because of post-concussion syndrome. style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Duff: It&#39;s painful for the Penguins and the league to think about, but post-concussion syndrome has brought an early end to many a great NHL career. It&#39;s time to wonder if Sidney Crosby might join that list.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/41518919/ns/business-media_biz/ target=blank >Newton shows media his workout routine</a><br/><p><a href=http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/41518919/ns/business-media_biz/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/newton workout football-4226126_v2.thumb.jpg alt=NFL draft prospect Cam Newton throws a pass while trainers and members of the media look on during a football workout Thursday, Feb. 10, 2011, in San Diego. (AP Photo/Chris Park) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Enjoying the San Diego sunshine and saying that he&#39;s shooting for greatness, Heisman Trophy winner Cam Newton gave the media a glimpse of the workouts he&#39;s going through daily as he prepares for the NFL combine and draft.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41510742/ns/sports-golf/ target=blank >McIlroy&#39;s 65 takes lead in Dubai, Woods shoots 71</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41510742/ns/sports-golf/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/dubai golf desert classic-188645314_v2.thumb.jpg alt=Tiger Woods plays a ball on 16th hole during the first round of Dubai Desert Classic golf tournament at the Emirates Golf Club in Dubai, United Arab Emirates, Thursday Feb. 10, 2011. (AP Photo/Kamran Jebreili) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Rory McIlroy upstaged the world&#39;s top three golfers with a 7-under 65 Thursday to take the first-round lead at the Dubai Desert Classic, four shots better than No. 1 Lee Westwood and Martin Kaymer and six ahead of an inconsistent Tiger Woods.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41351386/ns/sports-golf/ target=blank >Report: Woods got $55.4M to push golf resort</a><br/>DUBAI, United Arab Emirates (AP) -A United Arab Emirates business magazine says Tiger Woods received $55.4 million from a Dubai developer to promote a local golf resort which has yet to be built.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41516206/ns/sports-baseball/ target=blank >AL MVP Hamilton, Rangers reach $24M, 2-year deal</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41516206/ns/sports-baseball/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/rangers hamilton baseball--1204076464_v2.thumb.jpg alt=Texas Rangers&#39; Josh Hamilton smiles during a news conference announcing his new contract with the baseball club, Thursday, Feb. 10, 2011, in Arlington, Texas. Hamilton and the Rangers agreed to a $24 million two-year deal that avoids arbitration. (AP Photo) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Josh Hamilton walked through a gutted-out room under construction near the Texas Rangers clubhouse. The AL MVP had just agreed to a $24 million, two-year contract.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41514828/ns/sports-nba/ target=blank >Cavs&#39; Scott: &#39;I&#39;m the right man for the job&#39;</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41514828/ns/sports-nba/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/pistons cavaliers basketball--2629567_v2.thumb.jpg alt=Cleveland Cavaliers head coach Byron Scott watches in the fourth quarter in an NBA basketball game against the Detroit Pistons Wednesday, Feb. 9, 2011, in Cleveland. Cleveland&#39;s losing streak reached 26, matching the 1976-77 Tampa Bay Buccaneers&#39; record for consecutive incompetence on Wednesday night with a 103-94 loss to the Detroit Pistons, who were supposedly a beatable opponent for the bottom-dwelling Cavs. (AP Photo) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Cleveland coach Byron Scott is not concerned about his job security despite the Cavaliers&#39; epic losing streak.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41517132/ns/sports-nba/ target=blank >MJ practices with team; Wallace: &#39;He still has it&#39;</a><br/>Short on players for practice, the Charlotte Bobcats found an extra body in the front office: Michael Jordan.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41496195/ns/sports-nfl/ target=blank >Castrodale: Ready for a lockout, and not happy about it</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41496195/ns/sports-nfl/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/110209_spt-goodell-smith.thumb.jpg alt=NFL commissioner Roger Goodell and NFL Players Association executive director DeMaurice Smith will make fans quite unhappy if they can&#39;t reach a labor agreement, NBCSports.com contributor Jelisa Castrodale writes. style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Castrodale: As the NFL lockout looms, we can look to other sports to fill the void, but they are not football, and they are not enough to satisfy.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://profootballtalk.nbcsports.com/2011/02/10/league-should-be-blamed-for-breakdown-in-labor-talks/related target=blank >PFT: Blame NFL for breakdown in labor talks</a><br/><p><a href=http://profootballtalk.nbcsports.com/2011/02/10/league-should-be-blamed-for-breakdown-in-labor-talks/related><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/MSNBC/Components/Photo/_new/110210-goodell.thumb.jpg alt=PFT: The league should have acknowledged that 50 cents on the dollar is a reasonable opening position from the union and should have digested the offer and responded. style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>PFT: The league should have acknowledged that 50 cents on the dollar is a reasonable opening position from the union and should have digested the offer and responded.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41521215/ns/sports-motor_sports/ target=blank >Earnhardt reminders stir emotions in Waltrip</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41521215/ns/sports-motor_sports/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/nascar daytona 500 auto racing--1663102192_v2.thumb.jpg alt=Driver Michael Waltrip talks about the death of Dale Earnhardt in the 2001 Daytona 500 auto race during NASCAR media day at Daytona International Speedway in Daytona Beach, Fla., Thursday, Feb. 10, 2011. Waltrip won the 500 that year.(AP Photo/Terry Renna) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Michael Waltrip knew the questions were coming and tried to gather his thoughts in advance so he&#39;d be ready to answer. He even wrote about it in his book.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41521295/ns/sports-golf/ target=blank >Points thrives with Murray antics, leads at Pebble</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41521295/ns/sports-golf/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/pebble beach golf--2032037854_v2.thumb.jpg alt=Alex Cejka waits to hit from the tee on the eighth hole of the Monterey Peninsula Country Club course during the first round of the Pebble Beach National Pro-Am golf tournament Thursday, Feb. 10, 2011, in Pebble Beach, Calif. (AP Photo) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Some might argue that D.A. Points had the lowest score at the Pebble Beach National Pro-Am despite having Bill Murray as his partner.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41521090/ns/sports-baseball/ target=blank >LA Angels beat Jered Weaver in salary arbitration</a><br/>The Los Angeles Angels have defeated pitcher Jered Weaver in salary arbitration.</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41521205/ns/sports-baseball/ target=blank >Strasburg begins throwing in recovery from surgery</a><br/>Nationals pitcher Stephen Strasburg has begun throwing as he moves forward with his recovery from reconstructive elbow surgery.</p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/41516177/ns/health/ target=blank >Crosby wants to play again</a><br/>Crosby wants to play again</p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41514443/ns/sports-olympic_sports/ target=blank >Year later, luge world remembers Kumaritashvili</a><br/><p><a href=http://nbcsports.msnbc.com/id/41514443/ns/sports-olympic_sports/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/luger death one year later luge--865184251_v2.thumb.jpg alt=FILE - In this Feb. 11, 2010 file photo, Nodar Kumaritashvili practices for the men&#39;s luge at the Vancouver Olympics in Whistler, British Columbia. Saturday marks the one-year anniversary of Kumaritashvili&#39;s death in a training run on the opening day of the Vancouver Olympics. He&#39;ll be remembered at the site of this weekend&#39;s World Cup races in Russia with a brief ceremony.  (AP Photo/Elise Amendola, File) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>How it happened, that&#39;s no longer truly in question.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=newsAlt> <a class=newsLinkAlt href=http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/41510964/ns/health/ target=blank >Vonn becoming very cautious with her head injury</a><br/><p><a href=http://www.msnbc.msn.com/id/41510964/ns/health/><img align=left border=0 src=http://msnbcmedia.msn.com/j/ap/germany alpine skiing worlds--56785230_v2.thumb.jpg alt=Lindsey Vonn of the US finishes her run during the second training for the women&#39;s downhill, at the Alpine World Skiing Championships in Garmisch-Partenkirchen, Germany, Thursday, Feb. 10, 2011. (AP Photo/Matthias Schrader) style=margin:0 5px 5px 0 /></a>Cautious is usually not the best way to describe Lindsey Vonn.</p><br clear=all /></p><p class=news> <a class=newsLink href=http://matchups.nbcsports.msnbc.com/ALL/schedule/index.html target=blank >Matchups/injuries</a><br/></p></div> <p id=rsslink >Powered by: <a title=RSS-to-JavaScript.com: Free RSS to JavaScript Converter href=http://www.rss-to-javascript.com target=_powered alt=Free Content for Virtually Any Web-site! RSS-to-Javascript.com> RSS-to-JavaScript.com</a></font></p>');